<%# Each control posts its own change through the casting-source controller. %>
<div data-controller="casting-source" data-casting-source-update-url-value="<%= manage_casting_settings_path(@production) %>">
  <div class="max-w-3xl">
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-4">
      Choose where cast members for this production come from. Individual events can override this setting if needed.
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <label data-casting-source-target="option" class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 border rounded-lg cursor-pointer hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors <%= @production.casting_talent_pool? ? 'border-pink-500 bg-pink-50' : 'border-gray-200' %>">
        <input type="radio"
               name="casting_source"
               value="talent_pool"
               <%= 'checked' if @production.casting_talent_pool? %>
               data-casting-source-target="radio"
               data-action="change->casting-source#select"
               class="h-4 w-4 mt-0.5 accent-pink-500 cursor-pointer">
        <div class="flex-1">
          <span class="block font-medium text-gray-900">Talent Pool</span>
          <span class="block text-sm text-gray-500 mt-0.5">Cast from your production's talent pool members. Best for traditional casting workflows.</span>
        </div>
      </label>

      <label data-casting-source-target="option" class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 border rounded-lg cursor-pointer hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors <%= @production.casting_manual? ? 'border-pink-500 bg-pink-50' : 'border-gray-200' %>">
        <input type="radio"
               name="casting_source"
               value="manual"
               <%= 'checked' if @production.casting_manual? %>
               data-casting-source-target="radio"
               data-action="change->casting-source#select"
               class="h-4 w-4 mt-0.5 accent-pink-500 cursor-pointer">
        <div class="flex-1">
          <span class="block font-medium text-gray-900">Manual Entry</span>
          <span class="block text-sm text-gray-500 mt-0.5">Manually add anyone by name or email. Flexible for one-off events or guest performers.</span>
        </div>
      </label>
    </div>

    <!-- Casting Style Section -->
    <div class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Casting Style</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-4">
        How is a show put together — named positions to fill, or a running order of acts?
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <label data-casting-source-target="modeOption" class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 border rounded-lg cursor-pointer hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors <%= @production.role_based? ? 'border-pink-500 bg-pink-50' : 'border-gray-200' %>">
          <input type="radio"
                 name="casting_mode"
                 value="role_based"
                 <%= 'checked' if @production.role_based? %>
                 data-action="change->casting-source#selectMode"
                 class="h-4 w-4 mt-0.5 accent-pink-500 cursor-pointer">
          <div class="flex-1">
            <span class="block font-medium text-gray-900">Roles</span>
            <span class="block text-sm text-gray-500 mt-0.5">Fill named positions: Host, Performer ×6, Stage Manager. Best for plays, improv teams, crews.</span>
          </div>
        </label>

        <label data-casting-source-target="modeOption" class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 border rounded-lg cursor-pointer hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors <%= @production.act_based? ? 'border-pink-500 bg-pink-50' : 'border-gray-200' %>">
          <input type="radio"
                 name="casting_mode"
                 value="act_based"
                 <%= 'checked' if @production.act_based? %>
                 data-action="change->casting-source#selectMode"
                 class="h-4 w-4 mt-0.5 accent-pink-500 cursor-pointer">
          <div class="flex-1">
            <span class="block font-medium text-gray-900">Acts</span>
            <span class="block text-sm text-gray-500 mt-0.5">Build a running order: Magic, Clown, Intermission, Aerial… and cast each act. Performers can hold more than one act. Best for burlesque, variety, cabaret, circus.</span>
          </div>
        </label>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-3">
        Existing roles and assignments are kept either way. Switching to acts turns each multi-person role into one act per person (Dancer ×5 becomes five Dancer acts, cast kept) — rename them in the Lineup afterwards. Switching back to roles keeps every act as a role.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Event Defaults Section -->
    <div class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">Event Defaults</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-4">
        These defaults apply when creating new events. Individual events can override these settings.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between p-4 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg">
          <div>
            <p class="font-medium text-gray-900">Enable Attendance Tracking</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-0.5">New events will have attendance tracking enabled by default</p>
          </div>
          <label class="relative inline-flex items-center cursor-pointer">
            <input type="checkbox"
                   name="production[default_attendance_enabled]"
                   value="1"
                   <%= 'checked' if @production.default_attendance_enabled? %>
                   data-casting-source-target="attendanceToggle"
                   data-action="change->casting-source#updateSetting"
                   class="sr-only peer">
            <div class="w-11 h-6 bg-gray-200 peer-focus:outline-none peer-focus:ring-4 peer-focus:ring-pink-300 rounded-full peer peer-checked:after:translate-x-full peer-checked:after:border-white after:content-[''] after:absolute after:top-[2px] after:left-[2px] after:bg-white after:border-gray-300 after:border after:rounded-full after:h-5 after:w-5 after:transition-all peer-checked:bg-pink-500"></div>
          </label>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
